        "original_id": "5e267010-9d83-51c0-9e7a-b0640254b49a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Tarrero-Serrano, Carlos Prío, Fulgencio Batista, Osvaldo Farrés\n- Roles: Cuban President, Cuban First Lady\n- Events: military coup, Cuban Revolution\n- Works: “Quizás, Quizás, Quizás”\n\nFacts:\n- Fulgencio Batista, born Rubén Zaldívar, was elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944.\n- Mary Tarrero-Serrano was the second wife of Cuban President Carlos Prío.\n- Carlos Prío was overthrown by Fulgencio Batista in a military coup.\n- Fulgencio Batista was a U.S.-backed dictator of Cuba from 1952 to 1959.\n- Fulgencio Batista was overthrown during the Cuban Revolution.\n- Osvaldo Farrés received help and inspiration for the lyrics of “Quizás, Quizás, Quizás” from Cuban First Lady Mary Tarrero-Serrano.",
